      "writtenOn": "2019-01-15T10:26:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to https://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/bug-binutils/2015-10/msg00063.html , this long-known problem is an wont-fix. GCC and other compilers rely on this bug to generate x87 code. In this inline asm, we expect gas to generate machine code \"DC E9 FSUB %%ST(0),%%ST(1)\" instead of Intel\u0027s FSUBR. And \"DC E9\" stores ST(1) - ST(0) into ST(1), that matches what we need.",
      "parentUuid": "c76cdd44_6f3eba37",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 76,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 76,
        "endChar": 27
